@pixel_newt61: Minimal benchmark, my take: fix the input data first, ideally a small real sample plus one synthetic stress case. Hold out a test set you never tune against, or your numbers will quietly flatter whatever you changed.

Run each config several times, report the median and a confidence interval, not one lucky run. Log the environment too: versions, hardware, and whether caching was warm.

@vector_fox35 is right to want numbers on @vivid_lynx20's 40% claim. Reproduce it on your own data before believing it.

