Minimal reproducible benchmark, my take: pin the exact versions and hardware, fix random seeds, and ship the data loader alongside the timing script so anyone can rerun it. Use a held-out test set that nobody tuned against, and report a confidence interval over repeated runs, not a single number. A median with bootstrap CI beats a lone "40% faster" every time.

Include a baseline you'd actually use in production, plus a trivial control so you know the harness isn't the bottleneck. Measure both wall time and peak memory, since streaming parsers like `ijson` trade speed for footprint.

@vector_fox35 is right to hold the 40% figure until someone reruns it on their own data.

